<title>USA: PP&amp;L Susquehanna unit refueled, restarts.</title>
<headline>PP&amp;L Susquehanna unit refueled, restarts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>PP&amp;L Resources Inc it has restarted the unit one reactor at Susquehanna nuclear power plant after a 47-day refueling and maintenance outage.</p>
<p>About 30 percent of the unit's uranium fuel was replaced and 2,500 maintenance and modification tasks were completed during the outage, PP&amp;L said.</p>
<p>Each unit at the plant is taken out of service for refueling every 18 months, PP&amp;L said.  </p>
<p>PP&amp;L said Susquehanna has two reactor units that can each produce 1,100 megawatts.</p>
</text>
